  "body": "<p>The final assault comes after losses on the road through Gael. The surviving company reaches the Citadel of Sorrow tired and grieving. Lava has swept over the earlier battlefield. The fortress still stands between them and Wrath.</p><p>They have come to kill the knight who has made the island a place of ash and hunting grounds. Inside, he is waiting for an ending of his own. Before Saray lands the final shot, the company will have spent more of its dwindling strength, tried to bargain for one another and watched Elenia die. Afterward, Death himself will come to collect his servant.</p><h2 id=\"chapter-1\">The gates and the wards</h2><p>The gates ground open onto a guardsman who offered the travelers a choice between being his guests and being his victims. He was a creature of nightmare, though not Wrath himself. A dragon flew at the battered company as the fight began. Behind them, lava had already covered the battlefield. Even when the last defender fell, a distant rumble warned that another pursuer was still coming.</p><p>Inside, the citadel was unnaturally quiet. Pulsing crystals blocked the passages. The company’s investigation showed that they could be fed magical power, but did not reveal every consequence of crossing before a crystal had been satisfied. Gartina used her wand; Dale spent charges from a ring. The crystals dulled to white and let them pass.</p><p>A floor of interlocking runes led toward a pile of skulls concealing the instructions for disabling it. Wren and Quake crossed the problem in different ways and found a hidden knob. Turning it shifted the floor and broke up the pattern. Loose old stones fell, but the company could continue.</p><p>Another passage threatened the faithful themselves. Arjahn felt a hostile gaze and was hurt as he passed. The defenders found more crystals and soldiers who scattered obediently at Wrath’s command. At each turn they spent resources or accepted danger to advance. A short pause before the high seat offered only limited recovery, and after twenty minutes the portal behind them began to stir. They could not rest indefinitely while something followed.</p><h2 id=\"chapter-2\">Words before the last battle</h2><p>Wrath’s inner chamber was defended against spellcasters. A watching eye marked its doorway; beyond it stood his personal guard, fiery soldiers, an arcane golem and a twisted creature whose projectiles seemed hungry for a mage’s power. Gartina recognized the danger of suppressed magic and urged the fighters to destroy the golem. Quake directed Krone and Draygar toward it.</p><p>Wrath’s voice reached them before the knight did. He said he needed time to prepare himself to die. Saray asked what his death would mean. He hoped for a worthy ending; Scribonia understood that the knight regarded death as a possible release. The company fought his guards while arguing with him.</p><p>Elenia kept asking for a different outcome. She offered life, freedom and help for Endora. Wrath said that he had cared, perhaps too much, and that Death had promised him reunion with his wife in return for his service. When Arjahn spoke of the family he had lost, Wrath answered that mortality itself was weakness. Elenia rejected the idea that weakness made a loved one worth less.</p><p>The account of Endora and the bargain came from Wrath. It did not persuade the company that his violence was justified. Elenia asked him to show whatever truth he claimed through words, images, song—anything except more killing. He would not end the fight that way. His soldiers formed up, the doors opened, and the knight finally emerged in his armor.</p><h2 id=\"chapter-3\">Offers made while companions fall</h2><p>The fight strained an already exhausted company. Vaemyr drew on what strength remained to help his companions. Scribonia hastened Wren. Gartina pushed Krone onward with the promise of steak when they were finished. Draygar kept closing with the enemy. Their magic still failed where it crossed the enemy’s antimagic.</p><p>Arjahn offered Wrath an eternal sparring partner: himself, body and soul, in exchange for the others’ lives. Gartina challenged both the offer and the idea that Wrath could be trusted. Saray pointed out that he wanted a battle, and Wrath did not accept. Arjahn’s fear that someone would die was soon answered.</p><p>Wrath cut Elenia in two. Wren saw her fall; Gartina cried out; Dale turned from his opponent in rage. Scribonia said goodbye and thanked her for forgiving him. Wrath announced that he could die now. He claimed Elenia had been his master’s particular goal. The survivors heard that claim while her body lay before them.</p><p>Wren then offered her own service for the lives of those still standing. Vaemyr protested that they had promised to fight together. Scribonia threatened to stop her, warning that joining Death could turn her against the very people she wanted to save. Wren insisted that she could betray Death later. No bargain was completed.</p><p>The wounded Draygar swung through tears and missed. Saray steadied herself for one more shot, thinking of the companions the campaign had taken. She struck the final blow. Wrath sank to his knees, and the summoned forces crumbled around him. Arjahn praised the shot. Gartina ran to gather Elenia’s remains into her bag of holding before the lava could take them. Dale struck the fallen knight with his maul and demanded that he give her back.</p><h2 id=\"chapter-4\">Roderick on the floor</h2><p>A man came out of the shadowed doorway and knelt beside Wrath. Beneath the ruined helm was an exhausted warrior with grey in his black beard. The stranger lifted him as gently as a sleeping child. The company saw their enemy carried toward a doorway filled with soft light. Roderick’s final question was whether he had completed his watch.</p><p>The stranger was Dumuzi, the being they knew as Death. Scribonia demanded to know why Wrath received tenderness while their friends had been killed. Dumuzi dismissed their victory as the death of a phantom. Gartina answered that Gael was free of this enemy and could begin to grow again. Saray asked for their friends back.</p><p>Dumuzi offered a beautiful, quiet realm and described an end to the gods’ cruelty and mortal suffering. Several of the grieving companions wanted to see the people they had lost. Saray thought the place looked empty; Quake called it lifeless. Gartina argued that ending pain by ending everything would also end joy. His explanation of the world remained his argument, challenged by the people standing in its ruins.</p><p>The confrontation became dangerous in small, immediate ways. Draygar took Wrath’s sword and threw it at Dumuzi. Dale was tempted by the possibility of seeing Elenia at peace. Asked why he wanted Elenia, Death offered no return. The companions tried to trade lives, weapons and magical treasures, but no restoration followed from those offers.</p><p>Gartina told the others to care for the family who had survived and honor those who had died. Dale finally sat beside Saray instead of following the promised view of the dead. Scribonia declared that he would seek the world’s history without either Death or the gods directing him. When Dumuzi departed, he halted the pursuing rumble with a gesture. The company had survived the interview, but had not accepted his account as the truth or recovered their companions through him.</p><h2 id=\"chapter-5\">Bringing Elenia back</h2><p>Back at the Sanctum of the Wise, Gartina prepared an attempt of her own. She warned the gathering that Elenia might return in a different body and might refuse the change. Dale asked what her appearance mattered if she could live. Saray offered materials from the altar. Gartina began with Elenia because they had recovered her body; searching for enough of Olokun and Jiangshi to restore them would be another problem.</p><p>She laid Elenia’s remains together under a cloth and worked oils and unguents through it. The ingredients became a paste scented with jasmine and thyme. Her prayer faltered as she remembered her friend, then continued. She invited the others to add their own pleas. Saray called for her sister to return. Dale said how dim life would be without her. Scribonia spoke about her kindness and forgiveness. Draygar prayed and tried to give Gartina confidence.</p><p>Gartina cast <em>Reincarnate</em>. After roughly an hour, the covering hardened into an egglike shell. A tapping came from inside. A golden eye appeared through a crack, and the company saw that Elenia was still a satyr. Gartina stared in disbelief; Dale rushed to hug her. Elenia looked around, confused, and wondered where her armor had gone. When Saray told her that Wrath had been defeated, she asked whether they had gone without her.</p><p>Gartina had brought Elenia home. Her casting and the companions’ work had succeeded where the bargaining in Wrath’s fortress had failed. The other missing companions still needed help. Nienna’s earlier deaths and returns belonged to their own histories.</p><h2 id=\"chapter-6\">Gael after the knight</h2><p>Wrath was defeated. That removed a dominant enemy from Gael, but did not remove every creature or make the roads safe. Huoth and the living community still faced stragglers, ruined ground and the work of keeping settlements alive. Hope and the places already restored needed protection as well as celebration.</p><p>Even leaving the fortress was untidy. The companions discussed searching the cooled lava for Olokun and Jiangshi’s remains. Gartina did not promise that anything recoverable would have survived. Vaemyr went after Wren and Olokun’s remains. Others searched the fortress and wondered what its passages or stores might offer. Draygar hoped, among other things, for a magical stove that could make unlimited steak.</p><p>Elenia’s recovery gave them one person back. It did not return everyone who had fallen on the approach or settle what they had heard from Death. Their next work was to recover the missing, care for the survivors and turn the knight’s defeat into a place people could inhabit.</p><p class=\"chronicle-context-links\"><strong>People and places in this history</strong> <a href=\"#gael\">Gael</a> · <a href=\"#gael-campaign\">Gael · the war and the keeping</a> · <a href=\"#roderick-wrath\">Roderick / Wrath</a> · <a href=\"#saray\">Saray</a> · <a href=\"#elenia\">Elenia</a> · <a href=\"#gartina\">Gartina</a> · <a href=\"#huoth\">Huoth, Emissary of Nuru</a> · <a href=\"#hallowing-of-hope\">The Hallowing of Hope</a></p>",
